WEBVTT

1
00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.996
Quiet please, gentlemen.

2
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.708
After the extraordinary duel

3
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.672
of a theological nature,

4
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.628
produced by Father Oretti's words,

5
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.717
I give the floor

6
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.992
to Mr. Benito Mussolini,

7
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.599
a union representative

8
00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.911
and Socialist Party member.

9
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.554
Although of differing opinion,

10
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.799
it is correct to hear his opinion

11
00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.395
and let him express himself freely.

12
00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.359
I'll be brief.

13
00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.000
Does anyone have a watch?

14
00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.594
Don't worry, I'm not a thief.

15
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.833
It is ten past five.

16
00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.037
I challenge God!

17
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.029
I'll give Him five minutes
to strike me dead.

18
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.275
If He does not, it will be
the proof He doesn't exist.

19
00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.671
I'm ready.

20
00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.474
Time's up, God doesn't exist.

21
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.234
WIN

22
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.637
MILAN 1914

23
00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.471
Long live the Republic!

24
00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.473
A world of brothers,
in peace and freedom!

25
00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.031
Long live Socialism!

26
00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.510
Don't believe the Vatican nonsense.

27
00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.759
TRENT 1907

28
00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.952
We want justice on earth, here, now!

29
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.352
There can be no victory
without action, rebellion, violence.

30
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.951
Help me!

31
00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.071
No warring between peoples!

32
00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.669
Long live the Republic,
long live Socialism!

33
00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:12.235
Government rulers are arming for war.

34
00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.590
We want peace and justice.

35
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.991
Long live Socialism!

36
00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.353
Victor Emanuel, son of a murderer!

37
00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.118
Down with the King!

38
00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.112
The son of parasites!

39
00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.356
With the guts of the last Pope

40
00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.028
we'll strangle the last King.

41
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.588
Long live the Republic!

42
00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:47.359
MILAN 1914

43
00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.111
Remember?

44
00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:08.072
My love!

45
00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.678
I love you!

46
00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:18.869
SARAJEVO

47
00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:41.909
WAR!

48
00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:44.869
WAR!

49
00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.192
War!

50
00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.999
War!

51
00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:01.596
- Where are you going?
- I have to leave.

52
00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.389
I'll come too!
I have to see you again!

53
00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.108
Sure...

54
00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:08.391
Your laces are untied.

55
00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:38.117
...it'll start a national revolution,

56
00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:42.671
the bloody crown of Victor Emanuel,
the dwarf, will roll!

57
00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.711
I'm sorry, you can't go in.

58
00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:51.389
- You've sold out to the French!
- How much?

59
00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.791
History will prove I'm right.

60
00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:02.070
I'll be at your side
despite your insults,

61
00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:05.795
a revolutionary aims straight
to the goal, at all costs.

62
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.118
Turn in your Party card, you're
a disgrace to the Workers' Party.

63
00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:18.671
This isn't an assembly,
it's an execution.

64
00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:24.119
The Party has opted
for absolute neutrality.

65
00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.709
The Party is the people
and you've betrayed them.

66
00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:29.309
- Neutrality is for the castrated.
- What?

67
00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.351
Listen to me!

68
00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.758
You listen too, Benito.

69
00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:38.999
Proletarians don't want this war,

70
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.116
they don't want to get killed
for the middle-class.

71
00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:44.949
They think war is suicide.

72
00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:48.669
It's peace that gives bread.

73
00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:50.791
This war will kill all wars.

74
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.514
Middle-class slave!

75
00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.350
In July you said "down with war".

76
00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.871
I've changed my mind!

77
00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:03.554
Only mules never change paths.

78
00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:06.718
Besides, the middle-class
doesn't like my interventionism,

79
00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.070
they growl, accusing me
of recklessness,

80
00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:12.477
they're scared the armed proletarians
will turn against them.

81
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:16.719
This war, in which Italy must
absolutely not remain neutral,

82
00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:20.271
will turn the wheel of history
with its blood.

83
00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:21.993
It will be a revolutionary war.

84
00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:23.719
Peace is revolutionary.

85
00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.753
Don't forget Blanqui:
"Who has iron, has bread".

86
00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:27.995
And there's Napoleon.

87
00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:35.073
Don't be appalled if I say his name.

88
00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:38.317
Revolution is an idea
which has discovered bayonets.

89
00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:40.875
You hate me,
because you still love me.

90
00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.271
Take my arm.

91
00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.631
War!

92
00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.918
WAR
THE WORLD'S ONLY HYGIENE

93
00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.432
RALLY DON'T ROT

94
00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:26.392
In my youth I wanted
to be a musician or an author.

95
00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.040
But I knew I'd be mediocre

96
00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.435
and I'm terrified of time passing.

97
00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:41.754
You're the editor of Avanti,
you should be satisfied.

98
00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.076
I'll never be satisfied, never!

99
00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:46.671
I have to climb higher.

100
00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:49.989
I feel it my duty to be different

101
00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:53.192
from all who accept their mediocrity.

102
00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:56.438
The army of the virtuous
can't even imagine

103
00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.438
how this society
can be changed, revolutionized,

104
00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.756
moving beyond morality.

105
00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:06.832
That morality is my destiny.

106
00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.992
- Like Napoleon.
- Much more than Napoleon!

107
00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:13.472
He was a mere general! Napoleon...

108
00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.388
I've resigned from Avanti,

109
00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:23.029
they wanted me
to take a leave of absence.

110
00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:27.079
I'd tripled circulation,
that's why they wanted me to stay.

111
00:18:27.920 --> 00:18:29.911
I'll found a newspaper.

112
00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:34.630
I already have the title:
Il Popolo d'Italia.

113
00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:39.311
How?

114
00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:47.871
Luck goes past each man's door
at least once.

115
00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:51.272
You must open the door
to welcome it, at that very moment.

116
00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:22.637
When I see a priest,
I feel the need to wash my hands.

117
00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:23.319
Long live Italy! Down with Germany!

118
00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:29.235
War! Down with tyranny!

119
00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:32.913
Long live the national revolution!

120
00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.708
<i>Depart Italian soil,</i>

121
00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.075
<i>depart, the time has come,...</i>

122
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.560
<i>depart, all forelgners.</i>

123
00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.079
Ida?

124
00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:13.071
What happened?

125
00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:37.831
I sold everything.

126
00:22:40.440 --> 00:22:42.431
What do you mean?

127
00:22:42.760 --> 00:22:44.352
I sold everything.

128
00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:47.917
The apartment, the shop,
the furniture, the jewelry.

129
00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:53.792
For your newspaper.

130
00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:17.473
Take it.

131
00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:23.509
No.

132
00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:31.630
It's done, you have to take it.

133
00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.233
No.

134
00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:37.432
It's no sacrifice,
it's a joy, I love you.

135
00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:44.716
- It's a loan.
- Alright... a loan.

136
00:23:48.040 --> 00:23:50.031
I'll sign a receipt.

137
00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:52.271
- Later.
- Now.

138
00:23:59.280 --> 00:24:00.838
"I,

139
00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:03.918
Benito Mussolini,

140
00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:07.916
receive

141
00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.116
from Lady

142
00:24:11.360 --> 00:24:14.033
Ida Dalser

143
00:24:15.840 --> 00:24:17.831
the sum of..."

144
00:24:19.440 --> 00:24:21.749
I'll leave it blank.

145
00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:40.511
I'd say I have to marry you.

146
00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:44.110
Say "I love you" just once.

147
00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:26.912
AUDACITY!

148
00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:33.918
AUDACITY!

149
00:26:34.120 --> 00:26:37.669
Long live the War!
Down with neutrality!

150
00:27:40.520 --> 00:27:42.112
En garde.

151
00:27:56.320 --> 00:27:57.833
Doctor!

152
00:28:03.600 --> 00:28:05.875
The duel ends here.

153
00:28:06.640 --> 00:28:09.029
- Have you had satisfaction?
- No.

154
00:28:17.200 --> 00:28:18.997
Let them treat you.

155
00:28:19.200 --> 00:28:21.919
First I want to read the record.

156
00:28:37.920 --> 00:28:39.911
What happened?

157
00:28:40.680 --> 00:28:42.511
A duel.

158
00:28:47.080 --> 00:28:49.071
I have to talk to you, it's urgent.

159
00:28:49.840 --> 00:28:52.832
- Can't you wait?
- No, it's urgent.

160
00:28:54.120 --> 00:28:56.111
I have to talk to you right away.

161
00:29:02.360 --> 00:29:04.351
I'm pregnant.

162
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:20.673
Better a baptism than a funeral.

163
00:29:23.360 --> 00:29:24.429
Wait.

164
00:29:37.120 --> 00:29:39.953
A duel to the death,
to kill each other.

165
00:29:40.120 --> 00:29:42.998
They began before
the judge opened procedures.

166
00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:46.468
A blow to the ear, one to the arm...

167
00:29:46.680 --> 00:29:48.671
Mussolini wanted to kill him.

168
00:29:49.080 --> 00:29:51.071
It was brutal!

169
00:30:06.960 --> 00:30:09.758
Here's the text:
"Mussolini-Treves Duel".

170
00:30:09.960 --> 00:30:12.599
Mussolini's name must come first.

171
00:30:53.920 --> 00:30:55.911
Hurry, Rachele's here.

172
00:30:56.280 --> 00:30:58.271
- Who's she?
- Let's go!

173
00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:16.592
Go to Daddy.

174
00:31:16.800 --> 00:31:18.199
Edda!

175
00:31:19.520 --> 00:31:21.511
So much blood!

176
00:31:23.200 --> 00:31:25.191
A clean shirt.

177
00:31:26.600 --> 00:31:28.397
What did you do?

178
00:31:30.240 --> 00:31:31.878
You wanted to play hero.

179
00:31:38.640 --> 00:31:40.039
Give me a kiss.

180
00:31:40.320 --> 00:31:42.117
Another...

181
00:31:55.800 --> 00:31:58.678
ITALY DECLARES WAR
ON AUSTRIA-HUNGRY

182
00:31:58.880 --> 00:32:00.074
WE MUST WIN!

183
00:32:11.480 --> 00:32:13.710
Long live Italy!

184
00:32:24.440 --> 00:32:25.839
Long live war!

185
00:32:27.480 --> 00:32:28.469
War!

186
00:32:28.920 --> 00:32:30.273
Peace!

187
00:32:30.480 --> 00:32:32.948
War is the world's only hygiene.

188
00:32:33.040 --> 00:32:36.032
- Peace is the only solution.
- Shut up, draft-dodger!

189
00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:40.272
<i>Depart Italian soil...,</i>

190
00:32:52.120 --> 00:32:54.554
Long live neutrality,
long live Socialism!

191
00:32:54.760 --> 00:32:56.239
Long live the poor!

192
00:32:56.440 --> 00:32:59.318
You cowards, we're far more
Socialist than you.

193
00:32:59.520 --> 00:33:02.159
We're ready to die for Italy.

194
00:33:02.240 --> 00:33:04.390
Italy wants to go to war.

195
00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:05.799
Italy wants peace.

196
00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:08.594
You sold out to Germany and Austria.

197
00:33:08.800 --> 00:33:10.358
You sold out to France.

198
00:33:10.560 --> 00:33:12.551
- Italy's starving!
- You Judas!

199
00:33:14.000 --> 00:33:16.389
- Long live the working class!
- You're all clowns!

200
00:33:17.720 --> 00:33:18.948
You're corrupt!

201
00:35:36.120 --> 00:35:37.917
Latest news!

202
00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:43.434
Mussolini wounded
on the Carso Plateau.

203
00:35:52.360 --> 00:35:55.113
Mussolini wounded on the Carso.

204
00:37:21.040 --> 00:37:22.758
Turn the lights on!

205
00:37:24.040 --> 00:37:25.792
Right here, Your Majesty.

206
00:37:37.720 --> 00:37:39.711
How are you, Mussolini?

207
00:37:39.960 --> 00:37:42.394
You must be suffering.

208
00:37:44.520 --> 00:37:46.511
It's agony.

209
00:37:48.440 --> 00:37:50.351
But we have to hold out.

210
00:37:50.720 --> 00:37:54.110
General Olmi speaks highly of you.

211
00:37:55.280 --> 00:37:57.919
Thank you, Your Majesty...

212
00:38:00.720 --> 00:38:02.915
I just did my duty.

213
00:38:03.880 --> 00:38:09.796
Italy and the House of Savoia
are very appreciative.

214
00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:51.514
Why are you here? Go home, you spy!

215
00:38:51.720 --> 00:38:55.076
- I'm his wife.
- What? You brazen hussy!

216
00:38:55.280 --> 00:38:57.236
I'm his wife. Nothing to say?

217
00:38:57.440 --> 00:38:59.908
- Be quiet.
- Tell her I'm your wife.

218
00:39:00.920 --> 00:39:05.038
Don't forget your son,
don't abandon us.

219
00:39:10.240 --> 00:39:11.958
- Get out!
- Don't abandon us.

220
00:39:13.560 --> 00:39:14.754
Mad woman!

221
00:39:22.800 --> 00:39:24.233
I'm fine.

222
00:39:38.680 --> 00:39:42.070
I'll kill her, rip her ears off!

223
00:40:01.440 --> 00:40:03.908
You're my woman.

224
00:40:05.720 --> 00:40:07.711
You're my woman.

225
00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:12.111
So, be quiet.

226
00:40:16.880 --> 00:40:18.871
You're my little mouse.

227
00:40:31.240 --> 00:40:34.550
Kids, stop it
or we won't bring you anymore.

228
00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:43.278
Sit down!

229
00:40:47.040 --> 00:40:49.076
Sit in your seats.

230
00:41:04.960 --> 00:41:07.554
FUTURISTIC EXPO 1917

231
00:41:13.120 --> 00:41:14.917
Welcome, Mr. Editor.

232
00:41:15.120 --> 00:41:18.112
I'm honored and warfully happy
that you are here.

233
00:41:19.840 --> 00:41:21.831
Long live the Hero of Doberdٍ!

234
00:41:24.440 --> 00:41:27.273
The "rat-a-tat-tat"
of machine guns is a joy.

235
00:41:39.840 --> 00:41:42.832
Italy needs people
willing to risk their lives,

236
00:41:44.240 --> 00:41:46.117
to give blood for victory.

237
00:41:46.360 --> 00:41:48.351
It's the only direction for change.

238
00:41:48.560 --> 00:41:51.632
Futurism will explode
the depravity of our times.

239
00:41:51.840 --> 00:41:54.638
- Hurray for the war!
- Long live Futurism!

240
00:41:59.120 --> 00:42:02.635
You've realized the only
redemption is to win or die.

241
00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:25.319
- What's happening?
- A good deed.

242
00:42:26.960 --> 00:42:28.439
Benito, look at me.

243
00:42:34.120 --> 00:42:36.111
I'm ready to forgive you.

244
00:42:38.520 --> 00:42:41.080
Do what you like
but keep me with you.

245
00:43:02.440 --> 00:43:03.873
Get your hands off me!

246
00:43:19.480 --> 00:43:22.472
REVOLUTION IN RUSSIA

247
00:43:23.120 --> 00:43:26.556
POWER TO THE SOVIETS

248
00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:32.671
LENIN DICTATOR

249
00:43:32.880 --> 00:43:34.871
"Chaos in Russia"...

250
00:43:36.840 --> 00:43:38.831
or "Lenin dictator"?

251
00:43:44.520 --> 00:43:46.511
Come outside, you thief!

252
00:43:51.200 --> 00:43:54.636
You've abandoned your wife and son
to the deepest poverty!

253
00:43:57.640 --> 00:43:59.710
I've written to the Pope,

254
00:44:00.320 --> 00:44:04.279
the Prime Minister,
the Court of Milan,

255
00:44:04.560 --> 00:44:06.391
to the editor of
Il Corriere della Sera!

256
00:44:06.600 --> 00:44:08.591
So they'll send you to prison.

257
00:44:13.120 --> 00:44:14.633
You thief!

258
00:44:29.240 --> 00:44:30.639
WAR IS OVER!

259
00:44:33.520 --> 00:44:35.750
OUR MARTYRS HAVE ALL ARISEN!

260
00:44:37.720 --> 00:44:39.836
TRENT, TRIESTE AND UDINE FREED

261
00:44:42.360 --> 00:44:44.555
THE IDEAL HAS BEEN REACHED!

262
00:44:46.680 --> 00:44:48.671
RAISE HEARTS AND BANNERS ON HIGH!

263
00:44:50.880 --> 00:44:52.677
<i>Ministry of Internal Affairs</i>

264
00:44:52.880 --> 00:44:54.871
<i>February 13, 1920, Ida Dalser</i>

265
00:44:55.080 --> 00:44:57.116
<i>and her son Benito Albino Mussolini</i>

266
00:44:57.320 --> 00:44:59.117
<i>have been taken to the home</i>

267
00:44:59.320 --> 00:45:00.992
<i>of her sister Adele,</i>

268
00:45:01.200 --> 00:45:03.191
<i>who is married to Mr, Palcher,</i>

269
00:45:03.400 --> 00:45:04.799
<i>an accountant in Trent.</i>

270
00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:06.399
<i>Temporarily peaceful</i>

271
00:45:06.600 --> 00:45:08.272
<i>but with her propensity to flight,</i>

272
00:45:08.480 --> 00:45:10.357
<i>Ida Dalser is under</i>

273
00:45:10.560 --> 00:45:13.472
<i>strict surveillance night and day.</i>

274
00:45:13.680 --> 00:45:15.113
SOCIALIST FESTIVAL

275
00:45:15.320 --> 00:45:18.869
SOPRAMONTE, THREE YEARS LATER

276
00:46:16.280 --> 00:46:18.919
Ida, I'll put him to bed.

277
00:46:47.240 --> 00:46:48.434
Goodnight.

278
00:47:11.400 --> 00:47:12.958
<i>"My little Ida,</i>

279
00:47:13.120 --> 00:47:16.112
<i>I've just arrived after</i>
<i>an endless 12-hour train rlde.</i>

280
00:47:16.320 --> 00:47:19.790
<i>My first thought,</i>
<i>even before dining, Is for you, .

281
00:47:20.040 --> 00:47:21.632
<i>Happy?</i>

282
00:47:21.880 --> 00:47:24.553
<i>You say you love me</i>
<i>but I don't love you?</i>

283
00:47:25.560 --> 00:47:28.757
<i>I do love you, during the journey</i>
<i>I thought of you often, .

284
00:47:29.120 --> 00:47:33.113
<i>Every time a young married couple</i>
<i>or young lovers got on,</i>

285
00:47:33.360 --> 00:47:36.193
<i>I'd think about</i>
<i>the journey we'd planned.</i>

286
00:47:36.400 --> 00:47:38.231
<i>I'm your savage friend and lover."</i>

287
00:47:46.080 --> 00:47:48.548
- Adele, turn the lights off.
- What's wrong?

288
00:48:01.360 --> 00:48:03.999
<i>To arms, we're Fasclsts.</i>

289
00:48:04.200 --> 00:48:06.873
<i>We're the components of Fascism,</i>

290
00:48:07.720 --> 00:48:10.234
<i>and will support</i>
<i>the Cause to our death...</i>

291
00:48:22.440 --> 00:48:27.309
<i>..., its adversaries and traitors</i>

292
00:48:27.760 --> 00:48:30.320
<i>will be exterminated without mercy.</i>

293
00:48:31.080 --> 00:48:35.870
<i>To arms, to arms, we're Fascists,</i>

294
00:48:42.680 --> 00:48:43.874
Thank you, Ma'am.

295
00:49:23.560 --> 00:49:25.516
Madame President, good morning!

296
00:49:25.720 --> 00:49:27.392
Good morning, Madame President...

297
00:49:29.920 --> 00:49:31.114
That's enough!

298
00:49:36.240 --> 00:49:38.276
- Can you make the Fascist Salute?
- Yes.

299
00:49:38.480 --> 00:49:41.119
- Which hand is used?
- The left.

300
00:49:41.320 --> 00:49:44.118
The right! That's very important!

301
00:49:51.760 --> 00:49:55.878
THE GOVERNMENT PRESIDED BY MUSSOLINI
TOOK OFFICE YESTERDAY

302
00:51:14.080 --> 00:51:17.675
You went the wrong way, it's here.

303
00:52:19.000 --> 00:52:20.592
Are you cold?

304
00:52:30.920 --> 00:52:32.751
I saw Mussolini.

305
00:52:34.360 --> 00:52:35.918
On the movie screen.

306
00:52:36.120 --> 00:52:38.588
He's changed, he looks like a giant.

307
00:52:42.360 --> 00:52:44.920
He's lost lots of hair,
but his eyes are the same.

308
00:52:46.680 --> 00:52:49.114
I wrote him today too,
he'll answer sooner or later.

309
00:52:50.000 --> 00:52:51.991
You write to Mussolini...

310
00:52:53.640 --> 00:52:56.438
to the Pope, the King,
the Bishop, the Police.

311
00:52:58.040 --> 00:53:00.190
Have you ever had a single reply?

312
00:53:00.280 --> 00:53:02.794
He wants to punish me, but for what?

313
00:53:02.880 --> 00:53:04.950
Not even his lowest secretary
has replied.

314
00:53:05.840 --> 00:53:08.274
I've never betrayed him,
not even in thought.

315
00:53:08.480 --> 00:53:11.790
- That's bad, find another man.
- Either him or no one.

316
00:53:12.600 --> 00:53:14.113
I'm going to bed.

317
00:53:14.520 --> 00:53:17.080
Will he get my letters?
Will he know I'm alive?

318
00:53:17.680 --> 00:53:20.513
That his son attends a country school
and not the Royal College?

319
00:53:25.720 --> 00:53:29.349
Your son needs normality,
put your heart at rest.

320
00:53:30.840 --> 00:53:32.478
They call him a bastard.

321
00:53:32.680 --> 00:53:36.798
He's distracted, his grades are poor
but not due to a country school.

322
00:53:37.200 --> 00:53:38.997
His teacher hates him.

323
00:53:39.200 --> 00:53:41.031
She has nothing to do with it.

324
00:53:41.560 --> 00:53:44.472
We're watched day and night
like criminals.

325
00:53:44.680 --> 00:53:47.513
You think we are guarded
because you're Mussolini's wife?

326
00:53:47.720 --> 00:53:50.837
If the Carabinieri got the letters,
it might be different.

327
00:53:52.040 --> 00:53:55.032
The Carabinieri
swear loyalty to the King.

328
00:53:55.120 --> 00:53:58.396
Keep this up and
you'll lose your son.

329
00:53:59.400 --> 00:54:02.790
Today I barely managed
to keep custody.

330
00:54:03.640 --> 00:54:06.518
The judge knows me, but tomorrow?

331
00:54:10.120 --> 00:54:13.590
- They want him in another's care.
- Whose?

332
00:54:13.680 --> 00:54:15.716
- A Fascist, one of them.
- Who?

333
00:54:15.960 --> 00:54:18.918
- Magistrate Giulio Bernardi.
- That snake!

334
00:54:19.120 --> 00:54:21.793
Calm down,
they're all turning Fascist.

335
00:54:22.400 --> 00:54:24.789
I've been threatened
to be fired from the bank.

336
00:54:25.360 --> 00:54:27.032
Do we beg for alms?

337
00:54:27.240 --> 00:54:30.198
It's a lost battle,
they're stronger, resign yourself!

338
00:54:30.400 --> 00:54:32.197
I can't.

339
00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:35.991
I'm his wife.

340
00:54:37.040 --> 00:54:41.556
How can you think
I could adapt to a normal life?

341
00:54:43.000 --> 00:54:45.673
Only I understand him deeply,
because I love him.

342
00:54:45.880 --> 00:54:48.235
I'm convinced
he still loves me too,

343
00:54:48.440 --> 00:54:51.830
we have the same ideas,
the same principles.

344
00:54:51.920 --> 00:54:53.911
I was the first to believe in him.

345
00:54:54.120 --> 00:54:56.839
If he is what he is,
he owes some thanks to me.

346
00:54:59.080 --> 00:55:02.868
I'm the mother of his first-born son,
his natural heir

347
00:55:03.680 --> 00:55:06.672
who mustn't end up like the <i>Aiglon,</i>
the King of Rome.

348
00:55:07.280 --> 00:55:09.271
You don't even know French.

349
00:55:31.880 --> 00:55:33.632
Riccardo help me.

350
00:56:41.480 --> 00:56:45.268
Benito, there's just one shot here,
it's for your father's heart.

351
00:56:59.720 --> 00:57:02.154
Ida, it's time.

352
00:57:59.600 --> 00:58:02.034
Benito Mussolini,
do you take Ida Dalser

353
00:58:02.240 --> 00:58:04.310
as your lawfully-wedded wife...

354
00:58:14.320 --> 00:58:16.276
Yes, I do.

355
00:59:59.600 --> 01:00:01.511
Let me go, I have to play!

356
01:00:01.800 --> 01:00:03.518
Wait for me!

357
01:00:08.240 --> 01:00:10.037
Good morning, Ma'am.

358
01:00:16.800 --> 01:00:19.951
TODAY TRUSTED MINISTER IN TRENT

359
01:00:41.320 --> 01:00:43.311
Where are you going?

360
01:02:38.920 --> 01:02:42.913
...in the center
there's the altar of porphyry

361
01:02:44.240 --> 01:02:47.630
with the tomb of the hero,

362
01:02:48.680 --> 01:02:52.389
created by the sculptor Fozzer...

363
01:04:25.080 --> 01:04:26.798
She's crazy.

364
01:04:28.240 --> 01:04:31.391
We could write "paranoia syndrome".

365
01:04:32.880 --> 01:04:35.917
- She has a son.
- Too bad.

366
01:04:47.520 --> 01:04:49.795
The marriage certificate?

367
01:04:50.240 --> 01:04:52.800
- It's not here.
- I knew it!

368
01:04:54.560 --> 01:04:56.391
Bernardi, it's not here.

369
01:05:02.520 --> 01:05:04.317
How are you?

370
01:05:06.080 --> 01:05:07.798
Where am I?

371
01:05:14.840 --> 01:05:17.832
- In the hospital at Pergine.
- In the madhouse!

372
01:05:20.160 --> 01:05:22.958
"Abandon every hope
all who enter here".

373
01:05:23.240 --> 01:05:24.958
Quiet!

374
01:05:28.080 --> 01:05:31.197
Where are my clothes, my papers?

375
01:05:31.400 --> 01:05:33.436
The Police have them.

376
01:05:33.800 --> 01:05:35.791
I have to go home,

377
01:05:36.400 --> 01:05:38.391
my son is waiting.

378
01:05:39.680 --> 01:05:41.238
Are you deaf?

379
01:05:41.720 --> 01:05:44.712
My son is Benito Mussolini's
first-born son.

380
01:05:45.880 --> 01:05:47.871
Benito Albino Mussolini.

381
01:05:49.760 --> 01:05:52.228
I'm Benito Mussolini's wife.

382
01:05:52.440 --> 01:05:54.237
And I'm Napoleon's!

383
01:05:54.520 --> 01:05:58.513
- Shut up, or I'll tie you down.
- We are already!

384
01:05:58.720 --> 01:06:00.312
I'll put you in straight jackets.

385
01:06:00.520 --> 01:06:02.272
Fascist!

386
01:06:02.480 --> 01:06:05.392
<i>To arms, we're Fascists..., .

387
01:06:07.040 --> 01:06:08.234
That's enough!

388
01:06:08.440 --> 01:06:09.953
Stop it!

389
01:06:15.360 --> 01:06:18.875
I'm not joking,
I'll put you in isolation.

390
01:06:34.360 --> 01:06:37.875
Do you know Tatiana Pavlova,
the ballerina?

391
01:06:39.200 --> 01:06:42.192
She was my teacher
and a friend of Il Duce's.

392
01:06:43.800 --> 01:06:45.472
Write her.

393
01:06:52.080 --> 01:06:53.752
Stay still!

394
01:06:56.760 --> 01:06:58.159
Cover up.

395
01:06:58.360 --> 01:06:59.998
Be good!

396
01:07:01.840 --> 01:07:03.956
Don't make me be bad.

397
01:07:13.600 --> 01:07:15.750
No, stay down

398
01:07:16.760 --> 01:07:19.638
or they'll put you
in a straight jacket.

399
01:07:30.040 --> 01:07:32.076
You're beautiful.

400
01:07:34.960 --> 01:07:36.757
Is it true you're Il Duce's wife?

401
01:07:42.560 --> 01:07:44.551
How does Il Duce screw?

402
01:07:55.280 --> 01:07:58.431
"They were intent
in their boisterous pastime" comma,

403
01:07:59.200 --> 01:08:01.509
"in the golden peace
of the shadowed path..."

404
01:08:01.720 --> 01:08:03.233
Slowly.

405
01:08:05.800 --> 01:08:07.438
Comma.

406
01:08:07.960 --> 01:08:10.076
"...the two youths.

407
01:08:11.920 --> 01:08:16.391
In playing" comma
"as serious as if toiling"...

408
01:08:16.600 --> 01:08:17.919
Wait.

409
01:08:56.680 --> 01:08:58.079
Hello.

410
01:09:01.080 --> 01:09:04.072
- What's the matter?
- We have a search warrant.

411
01:09:04.280 --> 01:09:05.679
From whom?

412
01:09:05.880 --> 01:09:07.791
From the King's magistrate.

413
01:09:08.200 --> 01:09:10.191
We'll start upstairs.

414
01:09:12.960 --> 01:09:16.157
- Where's my sister-in-law?
- Is that a question to ask?

415
01:09:17.160 --> 01:09:19.390
Bernardi, don't you know anything?

416
01:09:21.280 --> 01:09:23.271
Adelina, take the child away.
